To create a shared component in Angular, you can follow these steps:

1. Create a new folder in the `shared` directory of your Angular project, for example, `components`.

2. Inside the `components` folder, create a new file for your shared component, for example, `my-shared-component.component.ts`.

3. In this file, define your component. For example:
```typescript
import { Component, Input } from '@angular/core';

@Component({
  selector: 'app-my-shared-component',
  template: '<p> {{ title }} </p>'
})
export class MySharedComponent {
  @Input() title: string;
}
```
This component will accept an input property `title` and will display it in a paragraph tag.

4. Now, you need to declare the component in the `shared.module.ts` file. This file should be created in the `shared` directory of your Angular project.

5. In the `shared.module.ts` file, import the `MySharedComponent` and add it to the declarations array.

```typescript
import { NgModule } from '@angular/core';
import { CommonModule } from '@angular/common';
import { MySharedComponent } from './components/my-shared-component.component';

@NgModule({
  declarations: [MySharedComponent],
  imports: [CommonModule],
  exports: [MySharedComponent]
})
export class SharedModule { }
```
The `mySharedComponent` will be available to use in any module that imports the `SharedModule`.

6. Now you can use the shared component in a different module. You need to import the `SharedModule` in the `app.module.ts` file (if you're using it in the app module) or in the module where you want to use the component.

Here's an example of how you can use the shared component in another component:

```typescript
