```
import React, { useState, useEffect } from 'react';

const Autocomplete = ({ options, onSelect, placeholder }) => {
  const [inputValue, setInputValue] = useState('');
  const [filteredOptions, setFilteredOptions] = useState([]);
  const [activeOptionIndex, setActiveOptionIndex] = useState(-1);

  useEffect(() => {
    const filteredOptions = options.filter((option) => {
      return option.toLowerCase().includes(inputValue.toLowerCase());
    });
    setFilteredOptions(filteredOptions);
  }, [inputValue, options]);

  const handleInputChange = (event) => {
    setInputValue(event.target.value);
  };

  const handleOptionSelect = (option) => {
    onSelect(option);
    setInputValue('');
  };

  const handleKeyPressed = (event) => {
    if (event.key === 'ArrowDown') {
      setActiveOptionIndex((activeOptionIndex + 1) % filteredOptions.length);
    } else if (event.key === 'ArrowUp') {
      setActiveOptionIndex(Math.max(0, activeOptionIndex - 1));
    } else if (event.key === 'Enter') {
      handleOptionSelect(filteredOptions[activeOptionIndex]);
    }
  };

  const renderOptions = () => {
    return filteredOptions.map((option, index) => (
      <div
        key={index}
        className={
          activeOptionIndex === index ? 'active-option' : ''
        }
        onClick={() => handleOptionSelect(option)}
      >
        {option}
      </div>
    ));
  };

  return (
    <div>
      <input
        type="text"
        value={inputValue}
        onChange={handleInputChange}
        placeholder={placeholder}
        onKeyPress={handleKeyPressed}
      />
      {filteredOptions.length > 0 && (
        <ul>
          {renderOptions()}
        </ul>
      )}
    </div>
  );
};

export default Autocomplete;
```
This component expects the following props:

* `options`: An array of options to autocomplete
* `onSelect`: A function to call when an option is selected
* `placeholder`: The text to display in the input field when no value is entered

The component uses the `useState` hook to store the current input value, filtered options, and active option index. The `useEffect` hook is used to filter the options when the input value changes.

The component renders an input field with a placeholder and an ul element to display the filtered options. When the user types into the input field, the options are filtered based on the input value. The component also handles keyboard events to navigate the options using the arrow keys and select an option using the enter key.

